# lsregsg.cf -- negative control for the EPSI1 patch in prn1_coeff()
# (t_pgen.c): Y = 2*X2 exactly here, so the fit is perfect (zero
# residual). This must still print "---" after the patch -- not via the
# rank check (the design matrix [1,X1,X2] is full rank: X1 and X2 are
# NOT collinear with each other, only Y is perfectly predicted), but via
# the separate, earlier check in lsreg() for near-zero total residuals
# (fabs(rnorme + rnorml) < ctx->EPSI1 forces cov = 0), independent of
# the se[j] threshold this patch changed. See lsregrd.cf/.ref for the
# rank-deficient negative control, and lsregsc.cf/.ref for the positive
# case this patch actually fixes.

nvar(
    dfile = singular.dat,
    X1 = c1,
    X2 = c2,
    Y  = c3,
);
lsreg (
) = Y,X1,X2;
